# Batch files must reach Windows with CRLF endings.
#
# cmd.exe reads a running .bat by byte offset rather than buffering the whole
# file, and its line accounting assumes CRLF. An LF-only batch file mostly
# works, and then does not: `goto` can resume mid-line, and a label at the end
# of the file can be missed entirely. update.bat is built out of labels, so it
# is the one most exposed to this.
#
# Stored as LF in the repository, checked out as CRLF everywhere.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# The rest is left to git's own detection, except where a byte-exact file
# would be corrupted by newline translation.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
